--- !u!1001 &1784921982
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 1541800528}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 707398162423377042, guid: 48422f878e71cc442931759086a044e1, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Padding.m_Bottom
      value: 450
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3169022222729764810, guid: 48422f878e71cc442931759086a044e1, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "<b><size=120%>Image Generation Instructions</size></b>\r\n\r\nWelcome
        to the <b>Image Generation</b> scene.  \r\nHere, for each object defined
        in the previous scene, a reference image will be automatically generated.\r\n\r\nPlease
        follow the instructions below:\r\n\r\n<color=yellow><b>1. Wait for Full Generation</b></color> 
        \r\nThe system will begin generating one image per object, as well as textures
        for the <b>floor</b> and <b>wall</b>.  \r\nThe interface will not be interactable
        until all images and textures have been generated.\r\n\r\n<color=yellow><b>2.
        Refining a Specific Image (Optional)</b></color>  \r\nOnce all images are
        visible:\r\n\n\u2022 You can <b>click on any image</b> to regenerate it. 
        \r\n\n\u2022 An <b>input field</b> will appear below every image.  \r\n\n\u2022
        If you enter a suggestion in the corresponding field (e.g., \u201Cmake it
        blue\u201D, \u201Cmore rustic\u201D), the image will be regenerated based
        on your feedback.  \r\n\n\u2022 If you leave the input field empty and click
        again, the system will regenerate the image <i>based on its own refinement
        logic</i>.\r\n\n<color=yellow> If the generated image contains backgrounds,
        multiple objects, or other unwanted elements, we recommend regenerating it
        and specifying in the input field that it should depict a single object on
        a plain background. </color>  \r\n\r\n<color=yellow><b>3. Proceed Only When
        Ready</b></color>  \r\nWhen you're happy with the results, click <b>Proceed</b>
        to move on to the next scene:  \r\n\U0001F449 <b>3D Scene Generation</b>.\r\n\n\n                                                              
        <b>PRESS X TO CLOSE</b>"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3350464789263833928, guid: 48422f878e71cc442931759086a044e1, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: Instructions
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4400144628398855194, guid: 48422f878e71cc442931759086a044e1, type: 3}
